    "narrative": "**Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (84.27) and **Bryce Harper** (80.21) anchor the lineup today, representing the clear elite-tier starts. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a massive matchup edge against Bratt, whose 6.32 xERA is the most exploitable figure on the slate, while **Bryce Harper** leverages a hitter-friendly park and a +16% park adjustment against Young. These two are the foundation for our offensive output today. We are also leaning heavily into favorable hitting conditions for **Taylor Ward**, **Dylan Beavers**, and **Tyler Freeman**, all of whom post strong scores above 68.00. **Dylan Beavers** in particular is a key play; despite a slight discount for an elite opposing catcher's pop time, his position atop the order and a +16% park boost against Painter make him a premier source of production.\n\nThe decision to bench **Kyle Karros** (59.60) was the most difficult call on the docket. While his 59.60 score sits just on the precipice of our \"Strong\" tier, he was edged out by the superior platoon and order-based efficiency of **Tyler Freeman** and **Daulton Varsho**. **Jonathan Aranda** and **Gleyber Torres** also force their way into the starting nine with high-60s scores, as both players benefit from significant SP skill and platoon advantages today. We are monitoring **Cal Raleigh** (58.29) closely; while he remains a start, his score is tempered by a negative park adjustment and a dynamic platoon disadvantage against the right-handed Matthews. If wind conditions shift or lineup changes shuffle the batting order, we may see some late-game volatility, but we are positioned to capitalize on the weak pitching matchups faced by our core sluggers.",
